USING THE PROGRAM (the installer "KDS-Lab-Desk-Setup.exe")
1. Free plan. The Owner allows any laboratory to install and use the unmodified
   program, free of charge, to approve up to 100 reports in each calendar month.
2. Licence. To approve more than that, the laboratory needs a licence code
   issued by the Owner. The Owner may charge for a licence and may set its
   limit and expiry date. K.D.S. Pathology holds an unlimited licence.
3. The program must not be modified, reverse engineered, or have its limit or
   licence check removed or bypassed, and it must not be sold, rented or
   redistributed except by the Owner.
4. Reports already approved can always be opened, printed and sent, whatever
   the plan.

THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
The program includes third-party components (for example Electron, Chromium,
pdf.js, qrcode, fflate, cfb, electron-updater, pino and Baileys). Each is
provided under its own open-source licence, which continues to apply to that
component. Their notices are included with the installed program (for example
LICENSE.electron.txt and LICENSES.chromium.html) and in each package's own
folder.

